From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:40:32 +0300
Subject: video: window framebuffer texture in ARGB8888/XRGB8888 on big-endian
 too

The accelerated window framebuffer (SDL_CreateWindowTexture) creates the
window surface in the texture's format and picked the renderer's first plain
format. The OpenGL and GLES2 renderers list only byte-order formats (BGRA32,
RGBA32, BGRX32, RGBX32): on little-endian the first is ARGB8888, on
big-endian it is BGRA8888 (bytes B,G,R,A). Applications that write
0xAARRGGBB words into the window surface without reading its format (OpenTTD
through sdl2-compat; SDL2 and the X11 framebuffer always gave them
ARGB8888/XRGB8888) then showed their alpha byte as blue: a strong blue cast
on the PS3 (ppc64, Mesa nv30), right colours with
SDL_FRAMEBUFFER_ACCELERATION=0.

Prefer ARGB8888 or XRGB8888 from the renderer's list, in its order (on
little-endian the same choice as before), and when the renderer has neither,
create the texture in XRGB8888 (ARGB8888 for transparent windows) and let the
renderer convert on update, like any texture in an unsupported format.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/video/SDL_video.c b/src/video/SDL_video.c
--- a/src/video/SDL_video.c
+++ b/src/video/SDL_video.c
@@ -413,20 +413,27 @@ static bool SDL_CreateWindowTexture(SDL_VideoDevice *_this, SDL_Window *window,
     SDL_free(data->pixels);
     data->pixels = NULL;
 
-    // Find the first format with or without an alpha channel
-    *format = texture_formats[0];
-
+    /* The window surface gets the texture's format. Applications commonly write
+     * 32-bit 0xAARRGGBB / 0x00RRGGBB words into it without looking at the format,
+     * as the unaccelerated framebuffers (XRGB8888) and SDL2 gave them, so prefer
+     * ARGB8888 or XRGB8888, in the renderer's order. The OpenGL and GLES2
+     * renderers list only byte-order formats (BGRA32, RGBA32, ...), which are
+     * ARGB8888 and XRGB8888 only on little-endian; on big-endian they are
+     * BGRA8888 etc. and the colours came out swapped. When the renderer has
+     * neither, create the texture in XRGB8888 (ARGB8888 if transparent) anyway
+     * and let SDL convert it on update. */
+    *format = SDL_PIXELFORMAT_UNKNOWN;
     for (i = 0; texture_formats[i] != SDL_PIXELFORMAT_UNKNOWN; ++i) {
         SDL_PixelFormat texture_format = texture_formats[i];
-        if (!SDL_ISPIXELFORMAT_FOURCC(texture_format) &&
-            !SDL_ISPIXELFORMAT_10BIT(texture_format) &&
-            !SDL_ISPIXELFORMAT_FLOAT(texture_format) &&
-            !SDL_ISPIXELFORMAT_INDEXED(texture_format) &&
-            (!transparent || SDL_ISPIXELFORMAT_ALPHA(texture_format))) {
+        if (texture_format == SDL_PIXELFORMAT_ARGB8888 ||
+            (!transparent && texture_format == SDL_PIXELFORMAT_XRGB8888)) {
             *format = texture_format;
             break;
         }
     }
+    if (*format == SDL_PIXELFORMAT_UNKNOWN) {
+        *format = transparent ? SDL_PIXELFORMAT_ARGB8888 : SDL_PIXELFORMAT_XRGB8888;
+    }
 
     data->texture = SDL_CreateTexture(data->renderer, *format,
                                       SDL_TEXTUREACCESS_STREAMING,
